{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125473-legacy-the-sympathetic-orneiromancer","id":1125473,"title":"Legacy: The Sympathetic Orneiromancer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T20:40:44-07:00","id":1125473,"title":"Legacy: The Sympathetic Orneiromancer","content":"So the Bene Ashmadi and Clavicalvarius seem to focus more on enslavement of goetia and beating them down by force. I kind of want to write a counter point to them, like a Legacy that focuses on Suppressing Vices and Conditions, focusing more on Clear Thoughts than Emotional Urging and kind of culminates in this &quot;Perfect Peace and Harmony&quot; thing, like the Indigo Tribe from Green Lanterns. Takes away their hate, their rage, their lust for other for goods for gold, just wants them to be calm and perfect. I may even have the Legacy itself seek sort of a collective Shunyata where those they guide are lead on a path of Vast Emptiness.<br /> <br /> The original concept focused more on the sort of Magical Therapist thing that actually struggled with their own Goetia to get their help corralling other people's Goetia. This is why I thought the Clavicalvarius would be a good fit. But I am not sure, now I am thinking this more Buddhist Absolute Bohdisattva type approach could be cool where other people around them start to lose parts of themselves as the mage themself obsessively tries grooming off the things that are hurting them.<br /> <br /> Ideas? Tips? Suggestions for Oblations or Yantra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8432-resilientcomma","name":"ResilientComma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:57:31-07:00","id":1125502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ResilientComma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1125473-legacy-the-sympathetic-orneiromancer#post1125473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Bene Ashmadi and Clavicalvarius seem to focus more on enslavement of goetia and beating them down by force. I kind of want to write a counter point to them, like a Legacy that focuses on Suppressing Vices and Conditions, focusing more on Clear Thoughts than Emotional Urging and kind of culminates in this &quot;Perfect Peace and Harmony&quot; thing, like the Indigo Tribe from Green Lanterns. Takes away their hate, their rage, their lust for other for goods for gold, just wants them to be calm and perfect. I may even have the Legacy itself seek sort of a collective Shunyata where those they guide are lead on a path of Vast Emptiness.<br /> <br /> The original concept focused more on the sort of Magical Therapist thing that actually struggled with their own Goetia to get their help corralling other people's Goetia. This is why I thought the Clavicalvarius would be a good fit. But I am not sure, now I am thinking this more Buddhist Absolute Bohdisattva type approach could be cool where other people around them start to lose parts of themselves as the mage themself obsessively tries grooming off the things that are hurting them.<br /> <br /> Ideas? Tips? Suggestions for Oblations or Yantra?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Bene Ashmedai already work with their Vices. However, there are apparently a ton of competing Legacies dealing with Goetia, so your flavor won't really be out of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T03:02:27-07:00","id":1127028,"title":"","content":"Well, if you want an Oneiromancer - one who reads the skein of dreams for prophecy - Mind/Time would probably work best.<br /> <br /> If you want a Legacy obsessed with performing emotional &quot;clean up&quot; and &quot;maintenance&quot; on other people and managing their lives for the better while also using Goetia I'd go with Mind/Fate.<br /> <br /> Do you have an idea for a parent order? Because that can help structure a lot of the philosophy. A Silver Ladder Order focusing on mental &quot;health&quot; is going to look a lot different than a Guardian of the Veil one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}